  "boundaries": [
    "Pending local future proof is separately indexed and bound to an exact new PROMISE/BASIS. Empty/legacy capture bytes and all packet/object/wrapper/image ceilings remain unchanged.",
    "The new independent process matrix derives actual stable-three EMPTY bootstrap and first BARRIER, actual original votes/application, future proof and exact captured/recovered bytes; it is not all-seven-profile acceptance.",
    "Fourteen halt/SIGKILL cases use 28 fresh JVMs and seven live lock probes. These process cuts are not power-loss evidence.",
    "Two separate Java source tests verify normal higher-ballot capture, duplicate/reopen immutability, holder/other-voter refusal before SELECTED and malformed source binding. Synthetic BASIS owners occur only in conditional negative fixtures.",
    "Final-source regressions separately cover existing local future transactions, selected-ledger installation, no-future original sources and pending-publication lifecycle. The legacy fourteen-case source matrix and nine negatives also replay unchanged.",
    "Normal, optimized and relocated original-first future-source replay agree, with ten exact evidence negatives. Nineteen focused Python regressions passed; this batch did not rerun all V5.3 Python suites or protected CI.",
    "Native selection and installation still refuse unresolved future references before SELECTED. This is temporary explicit integration scaffolding; selected proof ownership, carried entry application, future-target quorum and actual dispatch remain open.",
    "Full source/completion headroom before dispatch, automatic maintenance, the genuine offline-survivor history, learners/joint transitions and all remaining 3B\u20133E obligations remain required.",
    "No push, PR, workflow, paid cloud execution, public membership enablement or V5.2 Runner change."
  ],
